  13_ T3 s6         correct
  => 6 correct, 2 lost, 1 no-op-with-Success. Both failures are races on the same flag.

=== the MIRROR defect, from trial 2 ===
  Trial 2 opened with the twin wrongly holding s5 at is_up=0 while its process was running
  (leftover from trial 1's restore). 'power OFF s5' then returned {"192.168.123.15":"Success"}
  and killed NOTHING: the trial ended with 9 bmv2 procs, :30055 OPEN, :30056 closed.
  P4PowerStrategy::powerOff:180  ->  if (!topoMonitor->getVertexIsUp(node)) return success();
  P4PowerStrategy::powerOn:176   ->  if (getVertexIsUp(node) && !distrustWindow) return success();
  Both directions early-return Success on the same isUp flag, and B3 showed that flag is a
  record of commands rather than a measurement. So BOTH directions of the power API can
  report Success while doing nothing, in opposite circumstances.
  Trial 2 also shows the flag being re-raised by discovery: 5=0 -> 5=1 at t=1788369969.94,
  which is correct there (s5 really was running) and is the same writer that corrupts it in T1.
